#{[17592186489212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489212 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-1.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-2,-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a523061-b982-5542-a530-946bca7d0e33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489212 #edb/ref 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-2,-3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-2,-3)+∇f(-2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x+2,y+3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(-2,-3)=-19.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & ={y}^{2}\\, &  & ⇒\\,{f}_{x}(-2,-3)=(-3)^{2}=9, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =2xy &  & ⇒\\,{f}_{y}(-2,-3)=2(-2)(-3)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(-2,-3)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,-3) & =⟨9,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-2,-3)+∇\\,f(-2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+3⟩ \\\\  & =-19+⟨9,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+3⟩ \\\\  & =-19+9(x+2)+12(y+3) \\\\  & =35+9x+12y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489249 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489249 #edb/ref 1069 "q-65338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489249 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489249 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9d2fd7c0-6fec-5b30-98fe-3b0bf10ba9a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489249 #edb/ref 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,4,4)=\\frac{1}{6}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-\\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{2}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{108}, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =-\\frac{y}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =-\\frac{z}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,4,4)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,4,4) & =⟨{f}_{x}(2,4,4),{f}_{y}(2,4,4),{f}_{z}(2,4,4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{108}(x-2)-\\frac{1}{54}(y-4)-\\frac{1}{54}(z-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{1}{54}-\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{4}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}+\\frac{4}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489315 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489315 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "439f497b-63cd-56ed-a071-521a6753dfc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489315 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489322 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489322 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5ad6acc3-0cf4-512b-9839-fcc4716b1315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489322 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186404946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489323 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5e7f4e61-c58d-5ffd-a813-3c6ffee4ea99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489323 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489369 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489369 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d73be3e2-360c-5190-b3b2-da40bf0a43c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489369 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489376 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489376 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2dfefda-76b1-52f8-a7d5-688673b9ad6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489376 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425853 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
